  "notes": "The research calls him \"the lane's most influential programmer — syncopated 808 R&B with UK-garage-derived displacement\", 1997–2005. The spine is a \"**69 half-time spine** (counted 138) plus 88–93 straight\", so `halfTime` is true, the snare is `halftime_3` and the mode is 69. The board deltas are authored hardest, as a producer model should be. Gear and grammar are quoted: \"**Akai MPC60** for drums and bass; syncopated 808 kick displaced onto 16ths\" gives four to six kicks a bar at 0.8 syncopation — the highest in this section — with the secondary anchor on `2a`; \"hats programmed in gapped bursts\" gives a non-continuous 16th lane at 0.5 fill density with a 32nd-led ramped roll; and \"dynamics shifting 'back and forth' bar to bar\" is why the `velocityTiers` main band is unusually wide (70–96) under a 116–127 accent, and `velocityVar` sits at 0.26. His stated refusal — \"I've never been good at giving a 4–8 bar loop. I want to add colors and things that hit you\" — is `fills` every two bars and a `switchUpProb` of 0.6, the highest in the section, plus the arrangement rule that every section introduces something new. Harmony is the sourced progression: two-chord m9 vamps (`iv–i`), so ninth is the largest extension share at 0.52 and `adjacentSecondProb` is authored because he \"thinks in 'colors' added over a bed rather than in functional progressions\". The counter carries \"synthesized strings, 1970s wah-wah guitar licks, and unusual keyboard patches used as the hook\" at a 0.56 density. The low end is \"MPC-triggered 808 bass tuned to the vamp root, articulated in 16ths with short decay rather than sustained\" — articulated, not sustained, so it is the `bassline` block on `mirror_kick` and there is deliberately no `drums.bass808`, which would have silenced it. ⚠ The band is INFERRED around a single point: the entry gives a \"**69 half-time spine** (counted 138)\" and no half-time band, so the 64–80 cushion is this author's — asymmetric only so far as it stops short of the entry's separate \"88–93 straight\" material — and only the mode, 69, is the entry's own number. ⚠ The tonic set is part-sourced: \"C♯ minor, F minor, B minor\" are the entry's, and the fourth value, E♭ minor, plus all four weights are this author's. ⚠ The other INFERRED parameters are every velocity, density and jitter number and `swing.amount` 0.54.",
